<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03Z3">Notation <span data-tag="03Z3">8.5.1.27</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{Ret}$ denote the category introduced in Construction <a data-tag="03YB" href="/tag/03YB">8.5.0.2</a>. By construction, the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Ret})$ contains a retraction diagram $\sigma : \Delta ^2 \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Ret})$, which we depict as </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  \widetilde{X} \ar [dr]^{ \widetilde{r} } &amp;  \\ \widetilde{Y} \ar [ur]^{\widetilde{i}} \ar [rr]^{ \operatorname{id}} &amp;  &amp;  \widetilde{Y}. } \]
</div>
<p> We let $\mathcal{R}$ denote the image of $\sigma $, which we regard as a simplicial subset of $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Ret})$. </p>
</article>
